        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): harden embedded terminal policy",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFollow-up to #99918. The embedded operator terminal reached `main` while review was still in progress, leaving three correctness and safety gaps:\n\n- new tabs opened against the default agent instead of the currently selected agent;\n- tighter sandbox policy did not terminate already-running or in-flight PTYs;\n- terminal access and its relaxed WASM CSP were enabled by default.\n\nCloses #77362.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Make `gateway.terminal.enabled` explicit opt-in and drive RPC, Control UI bootstrap, document metadata, and CSP from the same effective launch policy.\n- Carry the active agent into each terminal tab and preserve that tab's agent identity for its lifetime.\n- Centralize terminal admission in a bounded launch-policy owner.\n- Stage cumulative restrictions before hot-reload work begins, terminate disallowed sessions immediately, and commit grants only after a successful reload.\n- Keep restart-bound grants and launch-detail changes unavailable until process replacement, while allowing revocations to take effect immediately.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators must set `gateway.terminal.enabled: true` to expose the browser terminal. Terminal tabs now use the active agent's sandbox and workspace. Tightening terminal or agent sandbox policy closes affected live sessions, and failed or ignored reloads cannot accidentally re-enable access.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-request-context.test.ts` — 2 files, 8 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/control-ui.http.test.ts` — 4 files, 236 tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox changed gate `tbx_01kwqb0hb0jwq50dwgnqkaex47` — types, core/UI/package lint, import-cycle and architecture guards passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28717780050\n- Blacksmith Testbox build `tbx_01kwqbgr2hn3w4fn58f4avxj3p` — core, runtime postbuild, plugin SDK export checks, and production Control UI build passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28718008674\n- Documentation formatting, MDX validation, and link audit passed with 0 broken links.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n- No package or lockfile delta. Post-validation rebase was patch-identical by `git range-diff`.\n",
